  "description": "MALNAS crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group I 2/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C46 H70 Cu5 Dy4 N8 O32,4(C2 H3 N1),1.5(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1A (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1D (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1D (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1E (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1E (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.061-5.328 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 74.84-177.71°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C46H70Cu5Dy4N8O32·4MeCN·1.5MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
